    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look primed for a productive outing, led by **Jackson Merrill**, whose 75.10 efficiency score marks the high-water mark for the day. Facing Trey Yesavage, **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a favorable matchup against a starter with a weak 4.55 xERA, and his projected batting order placement (#2) provides the necessary runway to maximize his counting stats. **Gunnar Henderson** (71.11) and **Kyle Tucker** (69.61) round out the top tier of our offense; while **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tough platoon disadvantage against Noah Cameron, the substantial park factor bonus elevates his overall ceiling. **Coby Mayo** (66.04) also capitalizes on that same environment, as the venue boost serves as the primary engine for his elevated projection.\n\nWhile we remain confident in our starters, the decision to leave **Miguel Vargas** on the bench was a tight call. His 51.83 score was bolstered by an excellent 0.398 xwOBA, yet he was ultimately edged out by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and others who offered better synergy with the projected lineups. The defensive battery of **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** remains a point of emphasis; although their statuses are still \"Lineup Pending,\" their scoring profiles reflect strong anticipation for them to hit in the top half of their respective orders. Managers should remain vigilant regarding **Jorge Polanco**, who remains on the bench not just due to a lower efficiency score relative to our starters, but also due to a 45% rain risk that introduces unnecessary volatility. We are holding a high floor across the board today, provided the weather in the midwest holds steady.",
